// A read method continues where the last read method on that File stopped,
// also on a path that cannot seek (spec/05-stdlib.md, File methods): /dev/stdin
// here is a pipe, so a seek cannot put back the bytes that a block read took
// past the line it returned. The File keeps them.
var f = open("/dev/stdin", "r");
var a = f.readline();
var b = f.readline();
print str(a) + "|" + str(b);
print f.read();
f.close();

// The bootstrap interpreter cannot run this probe: its wrapper feeds the
// program's source through standard input's own FIFO and forwards the caller's
// input behind it, so a program it runs cannot open /dev/stdin. The probe
// below checks what the bootstrap can reach: its File value is its host's File,
// so it reads lines one by one from a file it opens itself.
